<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Concession of Evoramonte</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1834</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Convention of Evoramonte, Convention of Évora-Monte · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liberal-wars">Liberal Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Concession of Evoramonte was the agreement of 26 May 1834 that ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liberal-wars">Liberal Wars</a> in Portugal. Defeated by the liberal forces of Pedro IV, the absolutist Miguel I surrendered at Evoramonte in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alentejo">Alentejo</a>, gave up his claim to the throne and went into permanent exile, receiving a pension in return. It restored Maria II as queen and secured the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitutional-monarchy">constitutional monarchy</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/concession-of-evoramonte.jpg" alt="Concession of Evoramonte" width="320" height="404" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Duque da Terceira · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Assinaturas_da_Conven%C3%A7%C3%A3o_de_%C3%89vora_Monte.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
